{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2021-12-06 08:30:00', 'title': "UPADACITINIB (RINVOQ®) ACHIEVED PRIMARY AND KEY SECONDARY ENDPOINTS IN FIRST PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDY IN PATIENTS WITH CROHN'S DISEASE", 'text': 'NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., DEC. 6, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- ABBVIE (NYSE: ABBV) TODAY ANNOUNCED POSITIVE TOP-LINE RESULTS FROM U-EXCEED, A PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDY, SHOWING UPADACITINIB (45 MG ONCE DAILY) ACHIEVED BOTH PRIMARY ENDPOINTS OF CLINICAL REMISSION A,B \xa0AND ENDOSCOPIC RESPONSEC AT WEEK 12.1 THE U-EXCEED STUDY ENROLLED PATIENTS WITH MODERATE TO SEVERE CROHN\'S DISEASE WHO HAD AN INADEQUATE RESPONSE OR WERE INTOLERANT TO BIOLOGIC THERAPY, WITH OVER 60 PERCENT HAVING PREVIOUSLY FAILED TWO OR MORE BIOLOGICS.1 U-EXCEED\xa0IS THE\xa0FIRST OF TWO\xa0PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDIES TO EVALUATE THE SAFETY AND EFFICACY OF\xa0UPADACITINIB\xa0IN ADULTS WITH\xa0MODERATE TO SEVERE\xa0CROHN\'S DISEASE.1\xa0 "THE DATA FROM THIS FIRST PHASE 3 INDUCTION STUDY IN CROHN\'S DISEASE SUGGEST UPADACITINIB MAY HELP ADDRESS THE NEEDS OF PATIENTS SUFFERING FROM THIS DISEASE, AS DEMONSTRATED IN STRINGENT ENDPOINTS SUCH AS ENDOSCOPIC RESPONSE," SAID MICHAEL SEVERINO, M.D.'}